    <statement><p>Find a vector parametric equation <m>\vec{r}(t)</m> for the line through the points <m>P = \left(-1,1\right)</m> and <m>Q = \left(-4,2\right)</m>.</p>
<p><m>\vec{r}(t) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Find a vector parametric equation <m>\vec{r}(t)</m> for the line through the points <m>P = \left(3,-4,5\right)</m> and <m>Q = \left(-2,-2,7\right)</m>.</p>
<p><m>\vec{r}(t) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>Find a vector parametric equation <m>\vec{r}(t)</m> for the line through the points <m>P = \left(-3,-2,4\right)</m> and <m>Q = \left(-7,-4,-1\right)</m>.</p>
<p><m>\vec{r}(t) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-1,1\right)+t\mathopen{}\left&lt;-3,1\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(3,-4,5\right)+t\mathopen{}\left&lt;-5,2,2\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-3,-2,4\right)+t\mathopen{}\left&lt;-4,-2,-5\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
